                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd173164-cc4f-433e-b06a-5abdc292d78d",
                                "sense_id": "7c2cdf69-ed47-33d1-8f35-47010bde89fb",
                                "text": "I did not see the message from Joe, when I began to make another attempt to collect a multilingual dict, which is now is included in the Debian Women Project [4] and in my homepage [5]. […] There currently are three sorts of dicts:\n - The acronym dict\n - Translations from and to English languages\n - Monolingual Dictionaries with explanations of words or phrases."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4cf17c1-bc93-416d-bc84-c88f3bffbfd7",
                                "sense_id": "7c2cdf69-ed47-33d1-8f35-47010bde89fb",
                                "text": "Other times, they combine words from one big dictionary with words from a smaller one. Steube was able to crack \"momof3g8kids\" because he had \"momof3g\" in his 111 million dict and \"8kids\" in a smaller dict."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
